Subject: [PATCH] Skip Xtensa cooperative yield helpers when icount is disabled

The cooperative high-priority IRQ helper returns without side effects when
icount is disabled. Avoid emitting its memw/retw calls in that mode, retaining
the memory barrier, register-window operations, retw helper and jump. Precise
and adaptive icount modes emit the original helper sequence, including replay
TBs which temporarily clear CF_USE_ICOUNT. The global icount mode is configured
before CPU execution; this does not add dynamic mode switching.

--- a/target/xtensa/translate.c
+++ b/target/xtensa/translate.c
@@ -20,40 +20,41 @@
